## Requests and your waiting list

People ask to be coached from your profile or an invite link, answering your questions. Their request
waits in Clients › Requests with their answers and a conversation. You see their answers and
nothing else until they're your client. Answer with:

- **Offer a spot.** Pick a package (or no payment through LogIt), how long to hold the spot, when they
  start and, for someone already paid up elsewhere, a later first charge. An offer holds one of your
  spots. You can change or withdraw it; if it runs out, Offer again.
- **Waiting list.** They're told in your conversation and can leave any time. Offer them a spot from
  Clients › Waiting list when one opens; nobody is offered one automatically.
- **Not a fit.** The request closes with your message. Tick Block for spam or abuse. Closed requests
  can be reopened from Closed.

Set your **client limit** at the top of Clients: clients and open offers each take a spot. When you're
full, your profile says "Join the waiting list", or "Not taking new clients" if you stop requests.
On the phone, requests are in Messages with the same three answers.

## Pausing or ending coaching

From a client's page, ⋯ › **Pause or end coaching**. **Pause** until a date when you're away, ill or
injured: their payments and check-ins pause, they keep training on their program, and it carries on
by itself on the date (or Resume coaching now). **End** stops their plan now: choose a refund (the
days not used, all of it, part of it, or none; it goes through your Stripe account from here), write
them a message, and suggest another coach if you like. They keep their program and history.

If a client has waited five days for a reply, Today says so. After seven days without one, they can
stop coaching with the unused days refunded.

## Away

Going away for a while? **Set away** from your account menu or ⌘K: the day you go, the day you're back,
and a note. The note is pinned in every client's conversation until you're back, and it ends by itself
on that day (or End now). Check-ins due while you're away aren't marked late, people who ask to be
coached see when you're back, and the seven-day clock starts again from your back-on day. Payments
carry on; to stop charging one client while you're away, pause coaching on their page. No automatic
replies are sent: the pinned note does that job.

## Sharing

Each client chooses what you see: workouts, nutrition diary, bodyweight, habits and check-ins. They can
change it any time; if they turn something off, that tab shows Not shared. Charts a client chooses to
show you appear on their Insights tab, and you can build charts for them too.

